//     compiler/05_emit.dag (T-10), compiler/02_parse.dag (T-7) —
//     emission and ingest are pipeline-stage operations, NOT facts
//     of this language file. The LanguageModel data DECLARES the
//     bidirectional rules; the pipeline stages EXECUTE them.
//     STOP-TRIGGER (named, binding): pre-D1 authoring of
//     `emit_rust : Node -> Outcome<RustSource>` here would parallel-
//     represent the Outcome carrier across every language file —
//     exactly the v3 cross-layer-drift failure mode the
//     keen-wren-419 STOP (T-4.6 formats, msg_0da56c18) foreclosed.
//     Defer-with-named-trigger, never stub.
//
//   - Rust ownership / lifetime semantic enforcement (the borrow-
//     checker rules — single-owner, exclusive-mutable, lifetime
//     well-scopedness): the OWNERSHIP LENS lens/ownership.dag (T-13)
//     CONSUMES the `RustReference` carrier declared here as the
//     structural fact it reads. Per THESIS:401 IN-B "effects are
//     intrinsic to the type signature, not an annotation layer" —
//     `&` / `&mut` / `'a` are STRUCTURAL Rust facts, not annotations;
//     they are declared here as the type-system surface and READ by
//     the ownership lens from the signature, never re-declared as a
//     parallel ownership taxonomy.
//
//   - Rust per-instruction cost INSTANCE-VALUES (concrete
//     `RustCost { instruction_cost: 1, allocation_cost: 0 }` rows per
//     operation): the carrier SHAPE is owned here (RustCost below);
//     concrete cost rows ride T-12 lens/cost.dag + U2 (the per-target
//     projection of U1's `Homomorphism<…, …, RustScalar>.map`). Pre-
//     T-12 instance-values would parallel-represent the cost the map
//     structurally encodes — the U1 no-engine smell (algebra.dag U1).
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag: `Node` (the bounded kernel's single recursive
//     type per A1; the `referent: Node` field on `RustReference`
//     carries the reference's TypeNoBounds per Reference §types-
//     pointer) and `Symbol` (the K-1 opaque kernel identity used
//     as the lifetime tag on `RustReference` + the segment carrier
//     for `RustVisibility.PubIn`'s SimplePath). Both are equality-
//     only at the boundary (Symbol's K-1 discipline); Node carries
//     its structural recursion through `children` per A1.
//   - std/logic.dag: `Bool` (KERNEL-AMBIENT — STRUCTURE.md
//     "Kernel-ambient types"; usable without an import, but
//     std/logic.dag is its sole modeling authority). The live
//     `IrToRust<Bool>` row references the type-parameter `Bool`
//     directly via the kernel-ambient resolution; no `import`
//     statement is needed (v2-compiler verifies 0-diag without
//     one). Naming std/logic.dag here makes the substrate-
//     authority dependency explicit; the absence of an `import`
