//   values carrying an opaque `Symbol` identifier per K-1). The
//   only `import` statements are `Node` and `Symbol` from
//   std/node.dag — driven by the `RustReference` Conj record's
//   `referent: Node` and `lifetime: Symbol` fields, plus the
//   `id: Symbol` field on `NamedSegment` (Node/Symbol are NOT
//   kernel-ambient, so they require explicit import even when
//   used in type-parameter / field-type position).
//   (The scaffold header's prior `std/node.dag, std/algebra.dag`
//   Consumes line was anticipatory — std/node.dag IS imported
//   (`Node` + `Symbol`, exactly as std/diagnostic.dag imports
//   `Node`); std/algebra.dag is NOT imported in this slice because
//   the inhabitance instance-values it would supply are DEFERRED
//   per D2 (so algebra.dag returns when D2 ratifies and the
//   inhabitance rows land here). The revised Consumes block
//   reflects what the file actually depends on, distinguishing
//   import-required (Node + Symbol) from kernel-ambient (Bool +
//   Int + List). Consumes correction rides the systemic operator
//   scaffold-Consumes reconciliation, T-4 mgr synthesis
//   msg_1fddb75c — the surface+trigger discipline lets the
//   operator ratify all per-file Consumes strikes uniformly in
